Theorem RL-102: Dispatch monotonicity

  Preconditions:
    - aims-proof/checker/src/checker.rs::check_proof_file is the
      top-level orchestration entry point per the proof-checker design
      sec-Architecture-Sketch
    - CoverageManifest loaded from checker/coverage-manifest.json
      maps each Category to an ordered list of engine names per the
      the proof-checker design sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory rows
    - each engine in aims-proof/checker/src/engine implements the
      Engine trait with accepts and dispatch methods per
      aims-proof/checker/src/engine/mod.rs
    - dispatch_theorem walks the manifest list in order and calls
      engine.dispatch once per engine per theorem
    - unimplemented_engine_shape is the verdict emitted when every
      engine in the manifest list returns EngineVerdict::UnimplementedShape

  Soundness property:
    Forall t in Theorem. Forall engines = manifest.engines_for t.id.category.
      dispatch_theorem t walks engines in declared order;
      each engine receives at most one dispatch call per t;
      no engine outside engines participates in the dispatch loop;
      when every engine in engines returns UnimplementedShape, the
        per-theorem verdict is UnimplementedEngineShape;
      when any engine in engines returns Fail, the per-theorem
        verdict is Fail and remaining engines are not dispatched.

  Proof obligation:
    Case analysis on the per-engine accepts and dispatch outcomes,
    combined with monotonicity over the dispatch sequence.

      Setup:
        Let engines be the manifest list for t.id.category. Let
        results[i] denote the EngineVerdict returned by engines[i].
        Define the per-theorem aggregate verdict over a prefix of
        results as the precedence Fail greater than UnimplementedShape
        greater than Valid; this corresponds to merge_results in
        aims-proof/checker/src/checker.rs.

      Case (engines is empty):
        dispatch_theorem returns UnimplementedEngineShape with
        engine equal to <dispatch> and reason citing the manifest
        empty list; no engine.dispatch call is performed.

      Case (engines has length N, every results[i] is Valid):
        dispatch_theorem walks every engine and returns Valid.
        Each engine invoked exactly once; no engine invoked twice.

      Case (results[k] is Fail for some k in 0 to N - 1):
        dispatch_theorem returns Fail with failing_engine equal to
        engines[k] and failing_theorem equal to t.id.canonical and
        reason equal to results[k].reason; engines at indices
        greater than k are NOT dispatched (early-exit per the
        dispatch_theorem loop body).

      Case (every results[i] is UnimplementedShape):
        dispatch_theorem returns UnimplementedEngineShape with
        engine equal to engines[0] (the first engine to declare
        UnimplementedShape) and reason equal to results[0].reason;
        every engine in engines is invoked exactly once.

      Case (mixed Valid and UnimplementedShape, no Fail):
        dispatch_theorem returns UnimplementedEngineShape with
        engine equal to the first UnimplementedShape engine.

    Monotonicity claim:
      The dispatch order is a left-to-right walk per the manifest's
      declared engine list. The verdict precedence
      Fail > UnimplementedShape > Valid is monotone with respect to
      prefix extension: extending a prefix by appending one more
      engine result never converts Fail into a weaker verdict; it
      may convert Valid into UnimplementedShape or Fail; it may
      convert UnimplementedShape into Fail. This monotonicity
      property is L-6-shaped (transfer functions are monotone) on
      the verdict lattice with carrier Valid <= UnimplementedShape <= Fail.

    Lattice validation:
      The verdict aggregation is a chain on the carrier
      Valid <= UnimplementedShape <= Fail (height 2). Monotone over
      prefix extension. Idempotent (calling merge_results twice with
      the same input produces the same output).

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (dispatch order invariant; verdict aggregation is
                    monotone over prefix extension)
      case_analysis (per-engine accepts truth-table enumeration; per
                     EngineVerdict variant enumeration)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: 01A bootstrap discharged via §01A Implementation Items (engine constructive verification + Lean 4 cross-validation)
